  "editorReview": {
    "text": "This book offers a genuinely useful framework for anyone tired of self-help clichés and seeking a systematic approach to change. Its core strength lies in moving beyond simple willpower narratives to treat personal growth as a design problem, a conceptual advance exemplified by its insightful analysis of 'instrumental burnout' in later chapters. The opening 'autopsy report' framing effectively sets the stakes. However, the reading experience can be uneven; the prose sometimes feels telegraphic or overly passive, and the structural clarity wavers in the final sections. It's best suited for read",
